==English==
[[File:Däumling.jpg|thumb|[[Tom Thumb]] stealing a pair of '''seven-league boots''']]

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun|head=[[seven]]-[[league]] [[boot]]s|sg=seven-league boot}}

# {{lb|en|folklore|fairy tale}} A pair of [[boot]]s enabling the wearer to cross seven [[league]]s at one [[stride]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Lady Anne Granard|page=211|volume=II|passage=The Count strode away as if he had secured '''seven-league boots''', and in less time than it seemed possible, though it was an age to Lady Anne (...), he returned with two bank of England notes in his hand, which he put into the bailiff's, saying,—"There's your money for yourself and all. You have proper behavour, and will make no say of this littel matter."}}

====Usage notes====
* The singular form is rare.

